cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Robust multi-objective low-Reynolds-number airfoil design"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline and config-driven tool for robust, multi-objective
  airfoil optimization at low Reynolds number, using AeroSandbox and the
  differentiable NeuralFoil surrogate, with manufacturing-tolerance robustness
  and independent XFoil validation. Includes a two-tunnel benchmark of
  NeuralFoil against 13,200 drag-run and 37,000 lift-run wind-tunnel points on
  94 airfoils (Re 30k-500k; clean, tripped and through stall) from the UIUC
  Low-Speed Airfoil Tests archive and the Princeton "Airfoils at Low Speeds"
  data set, including a tunnel-to-tunnel comparison and NeuralFoil run on the
  measured as-built model shapes, and an
  uncertainty-aware optimizer that uses the surrogate's measured reliability
  inside the design loop.
type: software
